{"content":[{"c":["EN-RIMMON"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Town assigned first to Judah and then to Simeon (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.32","r":"Josh.15.32","rawR":"Josh.15.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.32","value":"Josh.15.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:32"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.7","r":"Josh.19.7","rawR":"Josh.19.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.7","value":"Josh.19.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.32","r":"1Chr.4.32","rawR":"1Chr.4.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.32","value":"1Chr.4.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:32"},"). These verses refer to two places, Ain and Rimmon, but this was probably a scribal error for the one town, En-rimmon (see ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.7","r":"Josh.19.7","rawR":"Josh.19.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.7","value":"Josh.19.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:7"},"). It was resettled after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.29","r":"Neh.11.29","rawR":"Neh.11.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.29","value":"Neh.11.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:29"},"), and is perhaps the Rimmon south of Jerusalem mentioned in ",{"href":"?bref=Zech.14.10","r":"Zech.14.10","rawR":"Zech.14.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.14.10","value":"Zech.14.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zechariah 14:10"},". En-rimmon is thought to be the modern Khirbet Umm er-Rumamin, nine miles (14.5 kilometers) north of Beersheba."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"EnRimmon","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 15:32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.32","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.32","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.32"},{"anchorText":"19:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.7","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.7","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.7"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 4:32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.4.32","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.4.32","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.4.32"},{"anchorText":"Jos 19:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.7","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.7","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.7"},{"anchorText":"Neh 11:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.29","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.29","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.29"},{"anchorText":"Zechariah 14:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Zech.14.10","rawQueryValue":"Zech.14.10","sourceRefExact":"Zech.14.10"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"c2124703c989513630691f37c3a8cdd15e18de9ee48247eae8e8929a8a641e86","sourceItemName":"EnRimmon","sourceItemOrder":181,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"EnRimmon","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"En-Rimmon","title":"En-Rimmon","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}